 "briefing": "# Canva Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nNo verified, dated, and sourced changes at Canva in the 30-day window could be confirmed. Every search attempt returned no results, so this briefing contains no news, launches, hires, or deals. The gap reflects a failed search, not confirmed inactivity. Before the 17 November meeting, the items below should be checked directly at the primary sources.\n\n## News\n\nNo dated news items from 16 October to 15 November 2026 were verified. Canva's newsroom was not successfully reviewed.\n\n- **Check:** [Canva Newsroom](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/) for press releases dated in the window.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo product launches, AI features, integrations, or platform updates dated in the window were verified. Canva's blog and product pages were not successfully reviewed.\n\n- **Check:** [Canva Blog](https://www.canva.com/newsroom/news/) for product announcements, and Canva product pages for release notes.\n\n## Executive and Other Hires\n\nNo appointments, departures, or board changes dated in the window were verified. Leadership and LinkedIn sources were not successfully reviewed.\n\n- **Check:** The Canva company page on LinkedIn (People and Posts tabs) and the newsroom for leadership announcements.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo acquisitions, partnerships, investments, or customer or channel agreements dated in the window were verified. Partnership announcements often appear first on LinkedIn and in the newsroom, so both should be reviewed.\n\n- **Check:** The newsroom and tier-one business outlets (for example, Reuters, AFR, or TechCrunch) filtered to the date range.\n\n## Recommended Actions Before the Meeting\n\n1. Review the Canva newsroom and blog for the 16 October to 15 November 2026 period.\n2. Search tier-one outlets for Canva coverage in the window and record dates and URLs for each item.\n3. Check Canva's LinkedIn page for leadership and partnership posts.\n4. Confirm any findings against the primary source before citing them in the meeting.\n\n## Open Questions for Canva\n\n1. Which announcements from 16 October to 15 November 2026 should we treat as the most important updates, and where are they documented?\n2. Which product launches or AI features from this period are generally available, and which are still in beta or limited rollout?\n3. Have there been any senior hires, departures, or new partnership or channel agreements in this period that Canva would like to highlight?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Canva Newsroom: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/\n[2] Canva Blog: https://www.canva.com/newsroom/news/",
